# ym-mass-gap-lean-verification
**Lean 4 verification workspace for the Eriksson Programme on the 4D SU(N) Yang–Mills existence and mass gap problem.**

## Purpose

This repository is the main **Lean-oriented verification and formal architecture workspace** for the Yang–Mills mass gap programme.

It complements the companion repository:

- [`ym-audit`](https://github.com/lluiseriksson/ym-audit)

which contains the numerical, symbolic, and reproducibility audit suite.

## Mathematical claim

The underlying programme is presented as claiming a **mathematically unconditional solution, in the standard sense used by mathematicians**, of the 4D SU(N) Yang–Mills existence and mass gap problem.

Here, **“unconditional”** means:

- the proof does **not** rely on open conjectures;
- it no longer depends on the former “Hypothesis 1.1”;
- it is assembled from established inputs in the literature, including:
  - Bałaban’s renormalization-group results,
  - the Kotecký–Preiss cluster expansion,
  - Osterwalder–Seiler reflection positivity,
  - Osterwalder–Schrader reconstruction.

Using previously proved theorems as inputs is standard mathematical practice and does not by itself make a result conditional.

## Lean status

The current Lean layer is **modular and partially axiomatized**.

- Some analytic lemmas and logical assembly steps are formalized directly in Lean 4.
- Some established external theorems are currently represented as `axiom` declarations because they have not yet been fully ported into Lean/Mathlib.

Accordingly:

- **Mathematical status of the programme:** claimed unconditional.
- **Formal Lean status of this repository:** modular, partially axiomatized verification workspace.

